  "conclusions": [
    "No OOS month fell into the bottom 20% risk band under the baseline 48-month rolling calibration; 19 of 32 months were above the 80th percentile and 13 were middle. The low-risk reference group is absent, so a high-minus-low spread cannot be estimated.",
    "The baseline Spearman correlation between score and forward 12-month return is weakly negative; block-bootstrap intervals are wide and should be read as inconclusive.",
    "Across six fixed weight sets, the score-return rank correlation changes sign. The ranking is not robust to reasonable weight changes.",
    "The score-drawdown correlation is negative for all six weight sets, but the sample is short, the forward windows overlap and the association is not established as statistically reliable.",
    "Only eight OOS observations have complete 36-month forward outcomes, all overlapping; no 60-month OOS outcome is yet available.",
    "There are only three non-overlapping annual test anchors. This is insufficient for strong inference or strategy deployment."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The existing 120-month rolling factor percentiles and 36-month score history create a short effective sample despite a longer raw history.",
    "Forward 12-month outcomes overlap month by month. Moving-block bootstrap partially preserves serial dependence but does not create additional independent history.",
    "The test period begins after the 2022 rate-hiking cycle and is dominated by a particular macro regime; it does not include a broad set of independent cycles.",
    "The five weights were selected as transparent hypotheses, not fitted; sensitivity is a robustness check, not a search for a winning weight vector.",
    "Return series is the existing third-party Yahoo Finance-derived S&P 500 total-return proxy, USD; upstream redistribution rights are not independently verified.",
    "No transaction costs, portfolio weights, volatility targeting or asset allocation returns are evaluated. This is a signal validation, not a backtested tradable strategy."
  ],
  "next_requirements": [
    "Extend verified monthly total-return and macro histories while preserving point-in-time availability;",
    "Obtain enough post-training data to accumulate at least 8-10 non-overlapping annual test windows;",
    "Add ALFRED vintage data for revised macro series, particularly NFCI;",
    "Pre-register one primary outcome and one primary score specification before adding new test observations;",
    "Only then test portfolio overlays, turnover, costs, FX and drawdown constraints."
  ]
